rent event_prepare._ensure_initialized requires `.git` to exist. A `.git`-less dir carrying any non-dot subdir would now pass the write gate that previously rejected it. The plan's 'write gate does not loosen in practice' reasoning only addresses the mid-clone and live-store cases, never this one.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5e9732292118506e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix section — 'Both `_reads._tracker` and the write guard `event_prepare._ensure_initialized` call this ONE predicate'; WRITE AC 'rejects a mid-clone store and still accepts an initialized one'","norm_id":"n34d37a7b586c9e53","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A user runs a write against a directory that has a stray non-dot subdir (or a copied `.store-compat.json`) but no `.git` — previously rejected as 'not initialized', now passes the guard and fails deeper in git operations with a less clear error."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Have the write guard require clause 1 (`.git` + resolvable HEAD) and only reads accept clause 2's `.git`-less structure; or state explicitly that a `.git`-less structured dir on the write path is acceptable and add an AC pinning that behavior.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State a read-path latency expectation and specify predicate clause ordering (cheap filesystem structure check before the git HEAD subprocess) so normal reads do not fork a git process each call.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5a","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5a"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.884,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Fix: \"usable when isdir AND EITHER (1) .git present with a resolvable HEAD (git rev-parse --verify -q HEAD), OR (2) it carries the store STRUCTURE\"","\"a live store with event dirs already has a resolvable HEAD (clause 1)\" implies clause 1 (the git subprocess) is reached on normal live reads","Prior read behavior was `if not os.path.isdir(tracker)` — a pure stat with no subprocess"],"finding":"The read path (`_reads._tracker`) previously used a pure filesystem `os.path.isdir` check; the new predicate adds a `git rev-parse --verify -q HEAD` subprocess to clause 1, which for a live store (resolvable HEAD) executes on EVERY read. The plan bounds the call (run_git_bounded) but states no latency done-definition for reads and does not specify clause evaluation order (cheap filesystem structure check before the git subprocess) to avoid a git fork per read.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0f798eeea654b91d","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix section — \"The HEAD probe reuses the store's bounded runner gitutil.run_git_bounded\" / \"a live store ... already has a resolvable HEAD (clause 1)\"","norm_id":"n3bd83a002a826a9e","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Every read against a live store forks a git process; on a read-heavy caller (e.g. audit web index re-rendering or repeated gate-agent reads) this is one subprocess per read where there was previously none"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Evaluate the filesystem structure clause (2) first when it is definitive; reserve the git rev-parse probe for the ambiguous case, and add an AC asserting reads of a committed store perform no git subprocess (or a bounded latency target).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"64687b6550d5954f","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["26ae5e3aed8ea2c0",5601],"description_boxes":["05a8475feebbfea6",0],"file_impact":["5e2a0083b5c0a097",6],"ticket_id":["d0b409b5babd3489",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":4515.4,"input_tokens":870170,"llm_calls":28,"llm_ms":240193.8,"output_tokens":23952,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":257976.7,"verify_requests":11},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","priority_floor":0.8,"prov